# A `.view` result is read-only however the writer is written: a zero-argument
# method read as a member (`(xs.get i: 0).pop`) is a call of it, refused on a
# view result exactly as `(xs.get i: 0).append 1` is. Through `getMut` it runs.

main: function is {
    ys: List (ListVal i64)
    ys.append (ListVal i64)
    (ys.getMut i: 0).append 3
    (ys.get i: 0).pop
}
